# Conventions — quick nudges

Canonical sources, kept deliberately un-duplicated here:
[CONTRIBUTING.md](../../CONTRIBUTING.md) (how code is written here) and
[AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) (maintenance contract). Reminders:

## Writing code (`host/tmaze/**/*.py`)
- **It's an installable package `tmaze`** (under `host/tmaze/`, layered
  `core / io / vision / ui / tools`; see ADR-0083). Import package-qualified
  (`from tmaze.core import protocol`); launch as `python -m tmaze.<layer>.<name>`.
  Editable-install once per machine: `pip install -e .` from the repo root (also
  on each rig PC after a pull). No more "`cd host`, sibling imports".
- **Pure core + thin shell:** logic in stdlib-only, headless-tested cores under
  `tmaze/core/` (`protocol`, `maze_state`, `task_events`, `rules_engine`, and the
  `reward/ phase3/ session/ records/` clusters); Tk/OpenCV/serial in the shells
  (`tmaze/ui/*`, `tmaze/io/*`, `tmaze/vision/*`). Don't grow a GUI file with logic.
- **Placement rule (where a new module goes):** a *shell* layer
  (`ui` / `vision` / `io`) if it imports Tk/OpenCV/serial; else `core/` (+ the
  right cluster) if it's pure and headless-testable; else `tools/` if it's a
  standalone runnable. Cores must not import `io`/`vision`/`ui` — the
  `tests/test_architecture.py` boundary test enforces this.
- **Resolve paths via `tmaze.paths`** (`repo_root()`, `host_dir()`,
  `package_data()`) or `records.animals.resources_root()` for the sibling repo —
  never hand-rolled `os.path.dirname(__file__) + "/.."` hops (ADR-0083).
- Parse firmware lines via `tmaze.core.protocol`, reach the broker via
  `tmaze.io.rig_io`, guard optional deps via `tmaze.ui.gui_deps`.
- No magic numbers (named constant or `# see docs/decisions/NNNN`); comments
  explain why, not what; no new abstraction until 2–3 real callers.
- `tmaze.ui.maze_gui` and `tools/test_sensors_licks.py` are legacy — don't copy them.
- Any pure-core change ships a `tests/test_*.py`; run `run_tests.bat` (or
  `python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`) from `host/`.

## Keeping docs in sync (same change)
- New/changed runnable → update [PROGRAMS.md](../../PROGRAMS.md) (one line, exact command).
- Non-obvious decision → add an ADR (next free number; immutable — supersede,
  never rewrite) and reference it from code + commit.
- Deferred idea → add an `FW-NNNN` entry to [docs/future-work.md](../../docs/future-work.md).
- `docs/notes/` is the human's raw bug/idea inbox — you may read it and triage
  items out (promote real ones to `future-work.md`, remove fixed bugs), but don't
  require it to be tidy. See AGENTS.md "Triage the capture inbox".
